=== MIGRATION ===
File: internal/api/telemetry_handler_ingest.go
Function: normalizeFleetUnits (legacy MQTT-callback / debug-ingest path; not the
production normalize.Pipeline).

The legacy code dispatched compound-flattening through enums.SignalRegistry:
  info, ok := enums.SignalRegistry[name]
  switch info.Type {
  case enums.TypeDoors, enums.TypeTireLocation:
      flattenCompoundMapValue(...)
  case enums.TypeTime:
      flattenCompoundTimeValue(...)
  }

Replacement: explicit name-list switch matching the SAME 5 signals the
legacy SignalRegistry classified as TypeDoors / TypeTireLocation / TypeTime.
Verified against legacy signal_types.go: only DoorState (Doors),
TpmsHardWarnings + TpmsSoftWarnings (TireLocation), and
ScheduledChargingStartTime + ScheduledDepartureTime (Time) had those types.

Verified against protomodel.SignalsByName:
  DoorState                  ValueKind=ValueKindCompound
  TpmsHardWarnings           ValueKind=ValueKindCompound
  TpmsSoftWarnings           ValueKind=ValueKindCompound
  ScheduledChargingStartTime ValueKind=ValueKindCompound
  ScheduledDepartureTime     ValueKind=ValueKindCompound
All 5 are now first-class compound signals in the generated metadata, and
the production path through (*normalize.Pipeline).Process handles them
natively. The legacy normalizeFleetUnits keeps explicit handling because
its callers (cmd/teslasync MQTT subscriber, /telemetry debug ingest) still
operate on map[string]interface{}.

Other compound signals (e.g., Location at protomodel signal_metadata_gen.go:
ValueKindCompound) are intentionally NOT flattened by this legacy helper —
they have always been routed through the production pipeline only. This
matches the legacy behavior bug-for-bug since SignalRegistry never listed
Location.

