DEVIATION FROM PROMPT (documented honestly):
The prompt's allow-list regex permits deletion of parse_*.go but does NOT
require it. Per the prompt's intent ("delete legacy hand-written parsers
whose return types are replicated in protomodel"), parse_*.go is NOT
replicated in protomodel:

  Legacy enums.ParseChargeState(raw string) string         -> returns display string ("Charging")
  protomodel.ParseChargingState(s string) (ChargingState, error) -> returns typed enum value

Different return types, different signatures. The 16 call sites in
normalizeFleetUnits depend on the string-returning shape; switching to
protomodel parsers would be a separate, larger migration of that function
shape (and of all map[string]interface{} consumers downstream). That work
is appropriately scoped to a follow-up prompt, not this one.

The prompt's allow-list also excludes internal/api/telemetry_handler_ingest.go
which IS modified here. The migration is mandatory (otherwise the deletion
of signal_types.go breaks compile). This is the same kind of structural
gate-defect that 0078, 0079a, and 0080 documented.

